        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "bb16e8ca-0f80-524d-b974-202bdaaf0e83",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Edgar Ætheling, Cerdic of Wessex\n- Organizations: House of Wessex\n- Places: England, Britain, Wessex\n- Roles: King of England, founder, first king, leader\n- Concepts: Anglo-Saxon settlement, Anglo-Saxon Chronicle\n\nFacts:\n- Cerdic of Wessex is cited in the Anglo-Saxon Chronicle as a leader of the Anglo-Saxon settlement of Britain.\n- Cerdic of Wessex is described as the founder and first king of Saxon Wessex, reigning from 519 to 534.\n- Edgar Ætheling, also spelled Æþeling, Aetheling, Atheling, or Etheling, was born around 1051 and was the last male member of the royal House of Wessex.\n- Edgar Ætheling was proclaimed, but never crowned, King of England in 1066.\n- Edgar Ætheling was also known as Edgar II and died around 1126.",
